ding"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "_data": [], "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le10ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn7le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Mr Anderson, you are a specialist in the field of new technologies. Can you share with us which future developments you look forward to the most?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr Anderson</span>:    Without a doubt, I would say that Virtual Reality is going to change everything. With Virtual Reality, you'll put on a headset and find yourself in an alternate world. People are going to have experiences that they can't have in the real world, such as time or space travel. It will feel so real that they won't realize it's fake.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn7le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"time": "30600", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        Could you explain how users will get involved in the process?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr Anderson</span>:    Computer experts predict that Virtual Reality will take over television and video as the main source of home entertainment. In addition, they see important educational possibilities. In a biology lesson, for example, learners will be able to travel inside the body or inside plants. I'm developing a program like this next week.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"time": "56000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:        That sounds complicated, and expensive. Do you think that people will be able to afford the technology?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr Anderson</span>:    In the near future, everyone will be able to afford Virtual Reality. Experts predict that computer companies will give free equipment to people who subscribe to Virtual Reality services. Pilot programs are set to begin next year.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le10ob01re2img05.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}